Z||000000||Sndfr||12-22-2000||03:28 PM||||What's a <I>simple</I> engine swap into an '86 V6 automatic?  I have a high budget so don't worry about money.<P>I'm asking simple because I'm just starting to learn about car mechanics.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/scorchio/sevil.gif">  <B>Matthew "Whyt Nyte" D.</B>  <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/scorchio/sgrin.gif">       <BR><B><I>84 SE</B>- automatic, rare Fender Delete option<BR>"Fender gap?  What fender gap?"</I><BR><B>(future owner of a 60's-70's Chevy muscle car)</B><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/ut2/redcap.gif">                <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/ut1/mgwhore.gif"> ||||reg||2
Z||000001||1FST2M6||12-22-2000||03:29 PM||||HEH.. diveing right in hunh... simplist swap... uum a 3.4 probly (not the TDC) or to a 4cyl..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||12-22-2000||03:38 PM||||The simplest swap: is swap your old 2.8 with a new 2.8.  Unbolt old.  I'd get a new exhaust manifold or two (or Hedders). They tend to crack.  Upgrade injectors. Replace sensors, distributor, ignition module, wires, spark plugs, EGR pipe, vaccuum lines, water pump.  Any thing you can easily do to the engine with the new engine not installed.||||reg||3
Z||000003||mshill||12-22-2000||03:40 PM||||Definitely 3.4L OHV (92-95 Camaro).  But it's not too different than swapping in a new or rebuilt 2.8L.  I've rebuilt a 2.8L and am just finishing my 3.4L upgrade.  Since the 3.4L is nearly a direct replacement I really consider it more of an upgrade than a swap.<P>Some might say a 3.1 but again that is just rebuilding the bottom end of the 2.8.<BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||JohnnyK||12-22-2000||03:42 PM||||Of course, if your budget is that high, and you want to learn more quickly, opt for the 3.8  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||Sndfr||12-22-2000||04:10 PM||||Ok so what equipment changes from 2.8 to 3.4?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/scorchio/sevil.gif">  <B>Matthew "Whyt Nyte" D.</B>  <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/scorchio/sgrin.gif">       <BR><B><I>84 SE</B>- automatic, rare Fender Delete option<BR>"Fender gap?  What fender gap?"</I><BR><B>(future owner of a 60's-70's Chevy muscle car)</B><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/ut2/redcap.gif">                <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/ut1/mgwhore.gif"> ||||reg||2
Z||000006||Black88GT||12-22-2000||08:35 PM||||Just use the "search" function.  The 3.4 topic has been beaten like a dead horse||||reg||3
Z||000007||Will||12-22-2000||08:59 PM||||If you have a high budget, you can pay me to watch over your shoulder and offer helpful advice as you put a Norhtstar in your car.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>     I suppose I could be persuaded to let you watch while you pay me even more to put it in for you.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||WKDFIRO||12-23-2000||05:11 AM||||Changing to a V6 or anything other than a four cylinder is going to require just a little bit more for an 84 Fiero. The wiring connectors that the rest of us take for granted in 85-88 right next to the battery is just a little bit different than the rest. Some wiring is required. A former president of our club found out the hard way when he converted his 84 coupe into an 85 GT (complete with body panel swap.) The V6 harness won't just plug into an 84. At least not with a little bit of modification. Our former president is an electrical engineer so he was able to do it rather easily after he got the schematics. Wiring on that scale just frightens me...<P>He also found out the hardway about putting the wiring harness on the engine AFTER its put into the Fiero....<p>[This message has been edited by WKDFIRO (edited 12-23-2000).]||||reg||9
Z||000009||Sndfr||12-23-2000||02:09 PM||||I said an '86 V6 automatic, not my 84 SE.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||3
Z||000010||fieroshop||12-23-2000||03:33 PM||||The simplest eng swap/upgrade is the 3.4 engine from a 93-95 camaro/Firebird.<BR>We do this swap all the time and for the money it is the best.<P>------------------<BR> <BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroshop_sig_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||MachineHead||12-23-2000||04:40 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fieroshop:<BR><B>The simplest eng swap/upgrade is the 3.4 engine from a 93-95 camaro/Firebird.<BR>We do this swap all the time and for the money it is the best.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>How much do you guys charge?||||reg||1
Z||000012||88formula||12-23-2000||04:50 PM||||With the stock  automatic 2.8-liter fiero and a 3.18 final drive ratio your fiero goes 0-60 in 8.7 seconds and the quarter mile in 16.6 @ 84.3 mph. <P>With the stock 3.4-liter engine you car will go 0-60 in 7.26 seconds and the quarter mile in 15.43 seconds @ 91.9 mph.<P>Just to let you know what to expect in performance. With a highly modified 3.4-liter engine your fiero will go 0-60 on the low 6 seconds range and the quarter mile in the 14.3-14.5 second range.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 12-23-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||opm2000||12-24-2000||07:22 AM||||[QUOTE]Originally posted by 88formula: <P>With the stock 3.4-liter engine you car will go 0-60 in 7.26 seconds and the quarter mile in 15.43 seconds @ 91.9 mph.<P>   Then why bother with a 3.4 ?   Seriously, I rebuilt my '86 auto w/v6 and get 7.2 sec 0-60 every time, with a passenger along to handle the stopwatch.<P>   I did a fairly standard overhaul of the 2.8 using high compression pistons, and a mildly aggressive cam.   More info if you want it.<P><BR>||||reg||7
Z||000014||maninblack||12-24-2000||08:45 PM||||If your budget is high,might as well get<BR>an z06 engine and drop it in||||reg||1
Z||000015||WKDFIRO||12-25-2000||03:53 AM||||DOH!<P>In which case I agree with Fieroshop!<P>With money being no object it would be simple to simply add on the cam, the headers, the roller tip rockers, the hi-po valve jobs, match porting, and urethane during the process. Just as a beginning!||||reg||11
